    example: "While the vendor's voice-bot proposal rightly identifies learners' need for judgement-free daily pronunciation practice, its claim that automated bots can wholly replace live speaking instructors does not bear scrutiny. Current speech recognition struggles with regional Arabic accents in noisy rooms and cannot read subtle pragmatic discomfort or adapt cultural context spontaneously. A far more viable deployment would position voice drills as low-cost between-class scaffolding while preserving live human mentors for authentic dialogue and nuanced coaching.",
